--TEST--
`Core\Http\Method` declares exactly the eight verbs `rule:http-server/a-non-idempotent-retry-needs-an-idempotency-key` names, each a distinct integer constant, and the four CSRF enforcement covers are the contiguous tail — `rule:routing/route-attribute`, `rule:security/csrf-is-on-by-default`, `rule:enums/no-class-machinery`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:enums/core-enums
// The depth claim is *a bound asserted on both sides*, plus an invariance over
// a sweep: the last safe verb and the first unsafe one are named together by
// counting every safe/unsafe pair, so an enum that grew a case in the middle
// fails here while every individual line still reads plausibly.
//
// `rule:enums/no-class-machinery`: a case *is* its integer constant, so what a written case
// materializes is that constant — `nvs_stdlib::router::METHOD` is the table it
// comes from, and these are the values that table states.
array<int> $safe = [
    Core\Http\Method::Get as int,
    Core\Http\Method::Head as int,
    Core\Http\Method::Options as int,
    Core\Http\Method::Trace as int,
];

// `rule:security/csrf-is-on-by-default`'s set, in the order the enum declares it. CSRF enforcement is
// on by default for exactly these four, which is why they are a tail rather
// than four values scattered through the roster.
array<int> $unsafe = [
    Core\Http\Method::Post as int,
    Core\Http\Method::Put as int,
    Core\Http\Method::Patch as int,
    Core\Http\Method::Delete as int,
];

// 16 pairs, and the claim is that every one of them agrees: no safe verb's
// value reaches any unsafe verb's. A `Connect` case inserted anywhere, or a
// verb moved across the boundary, takes this off 16.
var $tail = 0;
foreach ($safe as int $s) {
    foreach ($unsafe as int $u) {
        if ($s < $u) {
            $tail = $tail + 1;
        }
    }
}
echo "tail=", $tail as string, "\n";

array<int> $all = [];
foreach ($safe as int $s) {
    $all = Core\Arr::append($all, $s);
}
foreach ($unsafe as int $u) {
    $all = Core\Arr::append($all, $u);
}

// 64 pairs, of which exactly 8 may be equal — each value with itself. Counted
// rather than read off eight lines, so two cases sharing a constant fails here
// however plausibly each prints on its own.
var $same = 0;
foreach ($all as int $a) {
    foreach ($all as int $b) {
        if ($a == $b) {
            $same = $same + 1;
        }
    }
}
echo "count=", Core\Arr::count($all) as string, " distinct=", $same as string, "\n";

// The far side of the same bound: eight distinct values spanning 0..7 is a
// dense range, so the roster has no hole a retired verb left behind.
echo "range=", Core\Arr::min($all) as string, "..", Core\Arr::max($all) as string, "\n";
--EXPECT--
tail=16
count=8 distinct=8
range=0..7
